  'weather-service-heatwave-alert-pretoria-34c-2026-11-12',
  'Weather Service heatwave alert sends Pretoria to 34°C',
  'Community', '2026-11-12', 'SABC News', 'https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/gauteng-heatwave-alert-remains-in-effect-as-temperatures-reach-34c/',
  'South Africa''s Weather Service kept its heatwave alert in force over Gauteng this week, with Pretoria reaching a high of 34°C on Thursday.',
  'The South African Weather Service''s heatwave alert for Gauteng took hold on Wednesday and was still active on Thursday, with Pretoria recording a high of 34°C, SABC News reported. Johannesburg reached 32°C and Vereeniging 33°C on the same day, the broadcaster said, as a ridge of high pressure kept the province hot and dry.

The Citizen reported that the weather service expected the heat to persist into Friday across southern Gauteng, the Free State and North West, with clear skies and little chance of rain. The outlook pointed to a very high ultraviolet index for the province and urged residents to limit time in direct sun during the hottest part of the day.

SAWS senior forecaster Tokelo Chiloane advised outdoor workers to wear protective clothing during the heat, SABC News reported. Residents were urged to drink plenty of water, stay in shaded or cool areas and check on children, older people and pets. Cooler conditions, with thunderstorms forecast, were expected to return to the region over the weekend.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/gauteng-heatwave-alert-remains-in-effect-as-temperatures-reach-34c/", "https://www.citizen.co.za/news/south-africa/weather/weather-forecast-11-november-2026/", "https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/11/heatwave-warning-pretoria-braces-for-three-days-of-intense-heat/"]',
  'agent'
);
